      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3271_Task4" name="Manage domain portfolio: register and renew BuildRight domains…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Manage domain portfolio: register and renew BuildRight domains (buildright.com.ph and variants, defensive registrations across TLDs, product/campaign domains per VS-75 digital engagement), DNS management, SSL/brand protection; align with brand launches (W3265)
Responsible (R): IP Counsel / IT
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3271_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3271_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3271_Task5" name="Monitor for digital IP abuse: watch for typosquatting, cybersquatting…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monitor for digital IP abuse: watch for typosquatting, cybersquatting, impersonating websites, phishing domains, unauthorized social-media handles/accounts (links to VS-14.2), counterfeit listings on marketplaces (links to VS-95); use brand-protection monitoring services
Responsible (R): IP Counsel / Security / Marketing
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3271_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3271_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3271_Task6" name="Enforce against digital abuse: send cease-and-desist, file UDRP/URS (via…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enforce against digital abuse: send cease-and-desist, file UDRP/URS (via accredited dispute-resolution provider) or IPOPHL cybersquatting action under RA 8293, takedown requests with registrars/platforms/social media, coordinate anti-phishing (links to VS-27.3/VS-86); update analytics (W3272)
Responsible (R): IP Counsel / External Counsel / Security
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3271_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3271_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
