    <bpmn:process id="W_W5563" name="W5563. Brand-Impersonation Commerce-Scam Response (Fake Sellers &amp; Fraudulent Pickup Offers)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Discovery that scammers are impersonating BuildRight to defraud consumers — fake &quot;BuildRight sale/clearance&quot; social-media pages and marketplace listings selling goods the scammers never hold, too-good-to-be-true offers with &quot;pickup at [BuildRight store]&quot;, fake promo/raffle pages harvesting personal data, or scam victims arriving at a store demanding goods they &quot;paid&quot; online
Frequency: Recurring brand-abuse class: several confirmed impersonation waves per year across social platforms and marketplace apps (Philippine online-shopping scam prevalence); a wave can spike sharply when a scam listing goes viral
Volume: 1 wave × the takedown surface (fake pages, listings, e-wallet handles) × victim contacts arriving at ~200 stores&#x27; service desks; the blast radius is brand trust and complaint volume, not inventory — the goods never existed
Owner: IP Counsel (event owner); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (enforcement posture)
Participants: Brand/Marketing (VS-14 advisory), Store Operations &amp; service desks (victim-arrival scripts), VS-27.3 (phishing-domain/infrastructure coordination), platform fraud channels &amp; marketplace IP desks, PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group (referral), VS-91 (breach assessment where personal data was harvested), Customer Service (VS-13), Talent Acquisition (W5557&#x27;s careers-site advisory where the wave touches hiring)
Source: workflow W5563 — Brand-Impersonation Commerce-Scam Response (Fake Sellers &amp; Fraudulent Pickup Offers)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5563_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5563_Lane1" name="Brand">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5563_Lane2" name="Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5563_Lane3" name="IP Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5563_Lane4" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5563_Lane5" name="VS-91">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5563_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5563_Start7" name="Discovery that scammers are impersonating BuildRight to defraud consumers — fake…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task8" name="Verify &amp; scope">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Verify &amp; scope: confirm the accounts/pages are not BuildRight&#x27;s (cloned logos, typo-squat handles); inventory the takedown surface; preserve evidence — URLs, screenshots, payment trails, victim reports
Responsible (R): Brand / IP
Accountable (A): IP Counsel
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task9" name="Victim-arrival protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Victim-arrival protocol: service-desk script live chain-wide — victims are treated as customers of a fraud committed against BuildRight&#x27;s brand: never blamed, given the advisory sheet, guided to the platform report channel, the same-day e-wallet/bank recall request, and the PNP Anti-Cybercrime referral
Responsible (R): Store Operations / VS-13
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task10" name="Public advisory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Public advisory: same-day advisory on official channels — BuildRight never sells via personal e-wallets or chat handles; the official store list and the verification page are the single source of truth; no engagement with scammers
Responsible (R): Brand / Marketing
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task11" name="Takedown wave">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Takedown wave: one simultaneous multi-surface report wave riding the W3271/W3272 machinery plus platform fraud/IP channels — registrar, marketplaces, social platforms, e-wallet providers — never filed serially
Responsible (R): IP Counsel / VS-27.3
Accountable (A): IP Counsel
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task12" name="Law-enforcement &amp; regulatory referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Law-enforcement &amp; regulatory referral: evidence pack to the PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group; DTI advisory-office coordination where a promo/giveaway scam is widespread
Responsible (R): Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task13" name="Data-harvesting variant">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Data-harvesting variant: where the fake page harvested personal data (fake raffle/promo forms), route to the W53 breach assessment — the NPC 72-hour clock applies from confirmation
Responsible (R): VS-91 / DPO
Accountable (A): Data Protection Officer
Duration: Per W53</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5563_Task14" name="After-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: After-action: wave post-mortem — verification-page discoverability, service-desk script refresh, platform-relationship notes, and W3271 watch-list tuning for known scammer handles
Responsible (R): IP Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 weeks post-wave</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5563_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5563_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5563_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5563_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-530 (ensure controlled execution — Intellectual Property Portfolio &amp; Brand Protection (PA-100.2).) | - operational: evidence preserved before takedown requests are filed; the advisory text approved by Legal before publication; victim-arrival scripts version-controlled and acknowledged by all service desks
Owner: IP Counsel (event owner); VP Legal &amp; Compliance (enforcement posture)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5563_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5563_Annotation16" targetRef="W5563_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5563_Flow18" sourceRef="W5563_Start7" targetRef="W5563_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5563_Flow19" sourceRef="W5563_Task8" targetRef="W5563_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5563_Flow20" sourceRef="W5563_Task9" targetRef="W5563_Task10" />
